            <ArticleTitle>[Crohn disease in pregnancy. Considerations on and discussion of a clinical case].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>339-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Crohn's disease with acute abdomen in pregnancy is described. The Authors evaluate Crohn's disease together with the diagnostic, prognostic and therapeutic problems and relationships between this disease and pregnancy. They conclude as underlining the rarity of Crohn's disease beginning in pregnancy and so the importance of symptoms related to this disease in fertile age woman to make diagnosis and therapy before pregnancy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
